Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Built-in STUN: bind to StunHost when it is a local
 address

On a multi-homed Windows PC (Ethernet + N2N/VPN adapter) a socket bound to
0.0.0.0 answered from the other interface's IP (10.10.0.2), and the game drops
STUN replies whose source is not the server it asked. Bind the primary socket
to StunHost when that IP belongs to this machine; otherwise keep 0.0.0.0.
Found in the real game, 2026-11-13.
---
 .../Matchmaking/BuiltinStunServer.cs          | 22 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Server-Infinite/Matchmaking/BuiltinStunServer.cs b/Server-Infinite/Matchmaking/BuiltinStunServer.cs
index 872d2b3..4ef4c22 100644
--- a/Server-Infinite/Matchmaking/BuiltinStunServer.cs
+++ b/Server-Infinite/Matchmaking/BuiltinStunServer.cs
@@ -38,11 +38,11 @@ public sealed class BuiltinStunServer : BackgroundService
