+## Real-game results (2026-11-13, times PT)
+Setup: two IB cabinets (POC) on one Windows 11 PC, each with its own IP and its own card server; cab1's card
+server (a second instance on another port) had `MatchUrl` pointing at the main server's `/match` (split setup), cab2 used the main server
+directly. Built-in STUN on the main server.
+* **Works:** RegisterPcb → SRV_MATCH + SRV_STUN; IssueNodeId; STUN NAT test; EntryMatching / CheckMatching;
+  per-mode queues (Mix Match world 23 and Class Match solo world 13 stay separate); in-game cancel
+  (CancelMatching); short-handed 1v1 room after `FillAfterSeconds`; the battle starts and finishes; each cabinet's
+  own card server got `SaveVsmOnResult` (HTTP 200) and stored class-match rate and badge.
+* **Split card server works:** a cabinet's card server can be a different server than the matchmaker (`MatchUrl`).
+* **Fixed – STUN source address:** on a multi-homed PC the built-in STUN socket bound to 0.0.0.0 replied from the
+  N2N adapter's IP; the game dropped those replies. Now bound to `StunHost` when it is a local IP.
+* **Fixed – badge exp:** a lost match took badge exp 0 → −20; now clamped at 0.
+* **FillAfterSeconds:** 30 felt slow; 3 works on a LAN; default now 15 (10–15 recommended for a public server).
+* **Open – results-screen hang** after every 2-cabinet **versus** match: both cabinets sit on the results screen
+  for minutes, then recover. Packet captures: every message answered, cabinets stay in sync, both card servers
+  answered 200. Holding Start does not clear it. CPU stand-in seats (`CpuStandInSeats`) reached both cabinets but
+  did not help. The same hang happens in **local LM mode with no matchmaker at all** (with two LMs and with one
+  shared LM); a solo route battle vs CPU does not hang. So it is **not caused by this server**; most likely two
+  game instances on one OS interfering. Pending: cab2 in Windows Sandbox (own network stack) and a real two-PC test.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
 * Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
