+## Online tag / partner recruit (2026-11-13, exvs2-lobbies `analysis/partner-invites.md`) — fake cabinets only
+How the game does "play with a specific partner from another shop" (オンラインタッグ, online tag), from static analysis:
+the partner relationship is a **tag team stored on the card server**; there is no in-game code entry. The cabinet
+lists the card's tag teams, the player picks one, and both cabinets search MMS **world 5** with
+`attr2 = pair key = min(own pilot id, partner_id)`; the lower pilot id is the leader. After the two cabinets find
+each other, they pair over P2P and only the **leader** sends a normal team entry (`groups=[partner]`, e.g. Mix 23 or
+Class 14), which matches like any other team.
+
+| Piece | What this patch does |
+|---|---|
+| Invite (WebUI **Teams** tab, re-enabled) | Player A enters partner B's **User ID** + B's **Invitation Code** → a tag team A+B on the server. The server now checks the code itself (upstream trusted the WebUI), refuses a team with yourself / a duplicate / more than 20 per card, and (default) B gets a new code after it was used (`OneTimeInviteCode`). A new team no longer crashes the tab (BGM 0). |
+| `LoadCard.MobileUserGroup.tag_teams` (36) | Filled for both partners: `id` = team id (same on both cards), `partner_id` = the partner's **pilot id** (= card id, the value the partner's cabinet uses as its own pilot id), `tag_status` = `OnlineTag.TagStatus` (default 0), partner name/level/class, `group_tag_point`. Log: `LoadCard online tag: CardId=… tag_teams=N … key K` |
+| Matchmaker world 5 (online tag) | **Pair** rule: exactly two solo cabinets with the same `(game, version, attr1, pair key)` → one room with both clients, **both group 0**, leader (lower am_id) first, the same list for both. Never short rooms, never CPU stand-ins; pair key 0 never pairs; NG lists (`bl_banapassport_am_ids`, `bl_loc_ids`), same card, same cabinet and network realms respected; the cabinet's timeout (90 s; 90 if it sends 0) then `MATCH_CANCELED`; cancel works as usual. Log: `MATCH room=… online-tag pair [n1,n2] key=K am=[a,b]`; `TAG-WARN` if the key is 0 or ≠ the lower am_id |
+| Worlds 21 / 22 (partner recruit 急募) | Same pair rule: 21 casual = one first-come pool, 22 ranked = keyed by team class (attr2). Lower node id first (the game's recruit leader rule is unknown). No widening across classes yet |
+| Team entries in worlds 5/21/22 | Refused (`ERR_MATCH_CONDITION`): those codes never send groups |
+| Team search after pairing | Unchanged team logic. A team entry that re-uses the node + apply_id of its finished pair search is no longer answered with the old 2-cabinet pair room |
+
+Config (`CardServerConfig.OnlineTag`):
+```json
+"OnlineTag": {
+  "SendTagTeams": true,       // fill LoadCard tag_teams (36)
+  "TagStatus": 0,             // TagTeamGroup.tag_status (meaning unknown): try 0, then 1 if the online-tag list stays empty
+  "MaxTeams": 20,
+  "OneTimeInviteCode": true   // the partner's invitation code changes after a team is created with it
+}
+```
+Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/OnlineTagTests.cs` (15) and `server-sketch/loadtest/online_tag_e2e.py` (card + WebUI
+API + MMS end to end, 28 checks). **Cross-card-server tags are not supported yet:** pilot ids are each server's DB row
+ids, so two servers' ids collide (partner-invites.md §6 Step C). Both partners must use the **same card server**.
+
 ## Real-game results (2026-11-13, times PT)
 Setup: two IB cabinets (POC) on one Windows 11 PC, each with its own IP and its own card server; cab1's card
 server (a second instance on another port) had `MatchUrl` pointing at the main server's `/match` (split setup), cab2 used the main server
@@ -138,3 +172,6 @@ directly. Built-in STUN on the main server.
 * Matchmaker state is in memory; restart drops waiting players (node ids persist, their polls get MATCH_CANCELED).
 * A room is never refilled or torn down when a member drops after the match: the protocol has no message for it.
 * Ranked results are saved per card (`SaveVsmOnResult`); a side that never reports simply records nothing.
+* Online tag / recruit: the CheckMatching shape the game expects for worlds 5/21/22 (2 clients, both group 0) is a
+  guess; `tag_status` meaning unknown; recruit leader rule unknown; tags only within one card server (ids collide
+  across servers). Untested in the real game.
